    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Logistic Regression Coefficients\n",
        "\n",
        "Each row of the Logistic Regression coefficient matrix corresponds to one predicted class. In this section, the plotted coefficients correspond only to Class 0.\n",
        "\n",
        "A positive coefficient means that a higher value of the transformed feature makes the model more likely to predict Class 0, while a negative coefficient makes Class 0 less likely.\n",
        "\n",
        "Because categorical variables were one-hot encoded, features such as `cat__cp_1` and `cat__cp_2` represent separate categories. These coefficients describe predictive associations in this dataset and do not prove that a feature causes heart disease."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "6nLboY_4_BGw"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Random Forest Model"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "UuWMwDttKRT7"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "from sklearn.ensemble import RandomForestClassifier\n",
        "\n",
        "# Create the Random Forest model\n",
        "rf_pipeline = Pipeline([\n",
        "    (\"preprocessor\", preprocessor),\n",
        "    (\n",
        "        \"model\",\n",
        "        RandomForestClassifier(\n",
        "            n_estimators=100,\n",
        "            random_state=42\n",
        "        )\n",
        "    )\n",
        "])\n",
        "# Train the model\n",
        "rf_pipeline.fit(\n",
        "    X_train,\n",
        "    y_train.values.ravel()\n",
        ")\n",
        "# Prediction\n",
        "rf_pred = rf_pipeline.predict(X_test)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "TQK8guKqKh9U"
      },
      "execution_count": 136,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "ConfusionMatrixDisplay.from_estimator(\n",
        "    rf_pipeline,\n",
        "    X_test,\n",
        "    y_test.values.ravel(),\n",
        "    cmap=\"Blues\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.title(\"Random Forest Confusion Matrix\")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.savefig(\n",
        "    \"random_forest_confusion_matrix.png\",\n",
        "    dpi=300,\n",
        "    bbox_inches=\"tight\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 472
        },
        "id": "ZytuXezfKou7",
        "outputId": "3842c671-5bbe-45e6-85f2-525ee239a1a6"
      },
      "execution_count": 137,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "display_data",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "<Figure size 640x480 with 2 Axes>"
            ],
            "image/png": "\n"
          },
          "metadata": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Observation:\n",
        "The Random Forest confusion matrix shows that the model correctly classified many patients in the majority class but still made errors for several minority classes. Some patients were predicted as neighboring disease categories instead of their true class.\n",
        "\n",
        "Random Forest captures more complex relationships than Logistic Regression, but multiclass classification remains difficult because the classes are not evenly distributed and some disease stages share similar characteristics."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "f5lFmAsUOSnI"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Random Forest Feature Importance"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "4We8qgSkOe3N"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "rf_model = rf_pipeline.named_steps[\"model\"]\n",
        "# Get the transformed feature names\n",
        "rf_feature_names = rf_pipeline.named_steps[\n",
        "    \"preprocessor\"\n",
        "].get_feature_names_out()\n",
        "# How important each feature is\n",
        "importance = rf_model.feature_importances_\n",
        "# Display each feature and its importance, larger number = the feature contributed more to making the data more pure when the trees were splitting the data\n",
        "for feature, score in zip(rf_feature_names, importance):\n",
        "    print(feature, \":\", round(score, 3))"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "n0IdT9NPOmNh",
        "outputId": "8d899fc2-40ca-4145-b5bd-bf724a811e71"
      },
      "execution_count": 138,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "num__age : 0.093\n",
            "num__trestbps : 0.081\n",
            "num__chol : 0.096\n",
            "num__thalach : 0.114\n",
            "num__oldpeak : 0.096\n",
            "cat__sex_0.0 : 0.016\n",
            "cat__sex_1.0 : 0.022\n",
            "cat__cp_1.0 : 0.012\n",
            "cat__cp_2.0 : 0.009\n",
            "cat__cp_3.0 : 0.014\n",
            "cat__cp_4.0 : 0.045\n",
            "cat__fbs_0.0 : 0.012\n",
            "cat__fbs_1.0 : 0.013\n",
            "cat__restecg_0.0 : 0.019\n",
            "cat__restecg_1.0 : 0.002\n",
            "cat__restecg_2.0 : 0.02\n",
            "cat__exang_0.0 : 0.033\n",
            "cat__exang_1.0 : 0.025\n",
            "cat__slope_1.0 : 0.024\n",
            "cat__slope_2.0 : 0.026\n",
            "cat__slope_3.0 : 0.007\n",
            "cat__ca_0.0 : 0.053\n",
            "cat__ca_1.0 : 0.024\n",
            "cat__ca_2.0 : 0.021\n",
            "cat__ca_3.0 : 0.019\n",
            "cat__thal_3.0 : 0.054\n",
            "cat__thal_6.0 : 0.008\n",
            "cat__thal_7.0 : 0.042\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Create a DataFrame\n",
        "importance_df = pd.DataFrame({\n",
        "    \"Feature\": rf_feature_names,\n",
        "    \"Importance\": importance\n",
        "})\n",
        "# Sort from highest to lowest\n",
        "importance_df = importance_df.sort_values(\n",
        "    by=\"Importance\",\n",
        "    ascending=False\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Display only the 15 most important transformed features\n",
        "top_importance = importance_df.head(15)\n",
        "# Plot\n",
        "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n",
        "plt.barh(\n",
        "    top_importance[\"Feature\"],\n",
        "    top_importance[\"Importance\"]\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.gca().invert_yaxis()\n",
        "plt.title(\"Top 15 Random Forest Feature Importances\")\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"Importance Score\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"Transformed Feature\")\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.savefig(\n",
        "    \"feature_importance.png\",\n",
        "    dpi=300,\n",
        "    bbox_inches=\"tight\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 451
        },
        "id": "LwBb59iZP5cT",
        "outputId": "ae8e38c9-1edd-4e71-b3aa-08115f7facfe"
      },
      "execution_count": 139,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "display_data",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "<Figure size 1000x600 with 1 Axes>"
            ],
            "image/png": "\n"
          },
          "metadata": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Observation:\n",
        "The feature importance plot shows that only a small number of features contribute strongly to the Random Forest model, while many other features have relatively low importance scores.\n",
        "\n",
        "The model relies more heavily on the most informative clinical features when making predictions. However, feature importance measures only how useful a feature is for prediction and does not indicate that the feature causes heart disease."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "l4GWjeTLQRU4"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Model Comparison"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Q5P5R3ddQRGY"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "#Calculate the value of 2 models\n",
        "from sklearn.metrics import (\n",
        "    accuracy_score,\n",
        "    precision_score,\n",
        "    recall_score,\n",
        "    f1_score\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Logistic Regression metrics\n",
        "lr_accuracy = accuracy_score(y_test.values.ravel(), y_pred)\n",
        "lr_precision = precision_score(\n",
        "    y_test.values.ravel(),\n",
        "    y_pred,\n",
        "    average=\"weighted\",\n",
        "    zero_division=0\n",
        ")\n",
        "lr_recall = recall_score(\n",
        "    y_test.values.ravel(),\n",
        "    y_pred,\n",
        "    average=\"weighted\",\n",
        "    zero_division=0\n",
        ")\n",
        "lr_f1 = f1_score(\n",
        "    y_test.values.ravel(),\n",
        "    y_pred,\n",
        "    average=\"weighted\",\n",
        "    zero_division=0\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Random Forest metrics\n",
        "rf_accuracy = accuracy_score(y_test.values.ravel(), rf_pred)\n",
        "rf_precision = precision_score(\n",
        "    y_test.values.ravel(),\n",
        "    rf_pred,\n",
        "    average=\"weighted\",\n",
        "    zero_division=0\n",
        ")\n",
        "rf_recall = recall_score(\n",
        "    y_test.values.ravel(),\n",
        "    rf_pred,\n",
        "    average=\"weighted\",\n",
        "    zero_division=0\n",
        ")\n",
        "rf_f1 = f1_score(\n",
        "    y_test.values.ravel(),\n",
        "    rf_pred,\n",
        "    average=\"weighted\",\n",
        "    zero_division=0\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "#DummyClassifier metrics\n",
        "dummy_accuracy = accuracy_score(\n",
        "    y_test.values.ravel(),\n",
        "    dummy_pred\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "dummy_precision = precision_score(\n",
        "    y_test.values.ravel(),\n",
        "    dummy_pred,\n",
        "    average=\"weighted\",\n",
        "    zero_division=0\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "dummy_recall = recall_score(\n",
        "    y_test.values.ravel(),\n",
        "    dummy_pred,\n",
        "    average=\"weighted\",\n",
        "    zero_division=0\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "dummy_f1 = f1_score(\n",
        "    y_test.values.ravel(),\n",
        "    dummy_pred,\n",
        "    average=\"weighted\",\n",
        "    zero_division=0\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "owtQ4ccbQ7B8"
      },
      "execution_count": 140,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Create comparison table\n",
        "comparison_df = pd.DataFrame({\n",
        "    \"Model\": [\n",
        "        \"Logistic Regression\",\n",
        "        \"Random Forest\",\n",
        "        \"DummyClassifier\"\n",
        "    ],\n",
        "    \"Accuracy\": [\n",
        "        lr_accuracy,\n",
        "        rf_accuracy,\n",
        "        dummy_accuracy\n",
        "    ],\n",
        "    \"Weighted Precision\": [\n",
        "        lr_precision,\n",
        "        rf_precision,\n",
        "        dummy_precision\n",
        "    ],\n",
        "    \"Weighted Recall\": [\n",
        "        lr_recall,\n",
        "        rf_recall,\n",
        "        dummy_recall\n",
        "    ],\n",
        "    \"Weighted F1-score\": [\n",
        "        lr_f1,\n",
        "        rf_f1,\n",
        "        dummy_f1\n",
        "    ]\n",
        "})\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "# Round the numbers to three decimal places\n",
        "comparison_df = comparison_df.round(3)\n",
        "comparison_df\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 178
        },
        "id": "E45bMMPXRvdJ",
        "outputId": "6132f9ba-09a3-4417-edd0-6f22d00cd794"
      },
